## Installation

This is a header-only library. Simply include the headers in your project:

### Option 1: Include Directly

Copy the `include/{{ project_name | snake_case }}` directory to your project and add to your include path.

### Option 2: CMake Integration

Add this library to your CMake project:

```cmake
# Using FetchContent
include(FetchContent)
FetchContent_Declare(
    {{ project_name | snake_case }}
    GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/Nathandona/{{ project_name }}.git
    GIT_TAG        main
)
FetchContent_MakeAvailable({{ project_name | snake_case }})

# Link to your target
target_link_libraries(your_target {{ project_name | snake_case }})
```

### Option 3: System Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Nathandona/{{ project_name }}.git
cd {{ project_name }}
cmake -B build
cmake --build build --target install
```

Then in your CMake file:
```cmake
find_package({{ project_name | title_case }} REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(your_target {{ project_name | title_case }}::{{ project_name | title_case }})
```

## Usage

### Basic Example

```cpp
#include "{{ project_name | snake_case }}/{{ project_name | snake_case }}.hpp"

using namespace {{ namespace_name | default(value = project_name | snake_case) }};

int main() {
    // Calculator operations
    auto sum = Calculator::add(2, 3);
    auto product = Calculator::multiply(4, 5);

    // String utilities
    std::vector<std::string> parts = string_utils::split("a,b,c", ',');
    std::string joined = string_utils::join(parts, " | ");

    // Container utilities
    std::vector<int> numbers = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
    bool has_three = container_utils::contains(numbers, 3);

    return 0;
}
```

{% if use_modules and cpp_standard == "C++20" %}
### C++20 Modules Usage

```cpp
import {{ project_name | snake_case }};

using namespace {{ namespace_name | default(value = project_name | snake_case) }};

int main() {
    auto result = Calculator::add(10, 20);
    return 0;
}
```
{% endif %}

## API Reference

### Calculator Class

Static utility functions for basic arithmetic operations:

```cpp
// Addition
auto sum = Calculator::add(a, b);

// Multiplication
auto product = Calculator::multiply(a, b);

// Division (with bounds checking)
auto quotient = Calculator::divide(a, b); // Throws if b == 0
```

### String Utilities

Functions for string manipulation:

```cpp
// Split string by delimiter
auto parts = string_utils::split("a,b,c", ',');

// Join vector of strings
auto result = string_utils::join(parts, ", ");

{% if cpp_standard == "C++20" %}
// Check substring presence (C++20)
bool found = string_utils::contains(text, substring);
{% endif %}
```

### Container Utilities

Generic container operations:

```cpp
// Check if container contains value
std::vector<int> vec = {1, 2, 3};
bool has_two = container_utils::contains(vec, 2);
```

## Testing

{% if include_tests %}
This project includes comprehensive tests using [Catch2](https://github.com/catchorg/Catch2).

### Running Tests

```bash
cmake -B build
cmake --build build
ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

Or run tests directly:
```bash
./build/tests
```

### Test Coverage

- Calculator operations with edge cases
- String utility functions
- Container operations
- Template constraints
{% if cpp_standard == "C++20" %}
- C++20 specific functionality
{% endif %}
